Sending engine
The sending process should be:
1.	Customer creates a campaign.
2.	System checks subscription and available credits.
3.	System checks audience permissions and suppression lists.
4.	System validates sender configuration.
5.	Campaign enters the queue.
6.	Laravel workers process batches.
7.	Provider sends the messages.
8.	Webhooks report delivery events.
9.	Dashboard updates campaign statistics.
Essential deliverability controls
•	SPF verification.
•	DKIM verification.
•	DMARC verification.
•	Bounce processing.
•	Complaint processing.
•	Unsubscribe processing.
•	Domain reputation checks.
•	Provider-specific rate limits.
•	Sending quotas.
•	Automatic campaign suspension when thresholds are exceeded.
Use a clearly visible unsubscribe link in marketing emails and automatically suppress recipients who unsubscribe. Support permission-based marketing and applicable privacy and anti-spam laws, including GDPR, CAN-SPAM, CASL and relevant local requirements.
Important business decision: Separate permission-based marketing campaigns from individually managed B2B sales outreach. Apply appropriate legal requirements to each. Do not allow purchased, scraped or otherwise unauthorized lists to bypass consent and suppression checks.
